ion_title":"An independent gradient argument below one half","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:80776a9c2596425fed9970643874ebeaecb82260f5fa043870b54fe99da36111","file":"preprints/Cutoff-throughout-the-high-temperature-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-phase-September-24-2026/build/appendices/introduction.tex","line":42,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ea420282720aa80991bdb179a15887ed75681383baf1c3fc631d91c0d0841aa9","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Cutoff-throughout-the-high-temperature-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-phase-September-24-2026/build/appendices/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:80776a9c2596425fed9970643874ebeaecb82260f5fa043870b54fe99da36111","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Cutoff-throughout-the-high-temperature-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-phase-September-24-2026/build/appendices/introduction.tex#L42"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{rcut:thm:main}\nFor every fixed $\\beta\\in[0,1/2)$, $\\varepsilon\\in(0,1/2)$, and\n$\\eta>0$, let\n\\[\n t_{n,\\beta,J}(\\varepsilon)=\\min\\{k\\ge0:d_d(k)\\le\\varepsilon\\}.\n\\]\nThen\n\\[\n \\P_J\\left\\{\n \\frac{t_{n,\\beta,J}(\\varepsilon)}\n {t_{n,\\beta,J}(1-\\varepsilon)}>1+\\eta\\right\\}\\longrightarrow0.\n\\]\nThe denominator is positive for sufficiently large $n$."}
